msgid "At {clueCount} clues out of 81 cells, this booklet is the first one worth solving with a pencil. Singles carry a Medium grid part of the way, but every puzzle in it provably stalls on them — that is the test each board had to fail to be printed here — until you spot a <0>pointing pair</0> or a <1>box-line reduction</1>, an intersection between a box and a line that only eliminates candidates, never places a digit outright. Nothing in the booklet needs a fish, a wing or a chain."
